cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SKaiNET in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
title: "SKaiNET: A Kotlin Multiplatform AI Framework"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Harakal
    given-names: Michal
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7981-4075
  - name: SKaiNET-developers contributors
    website: https://github.com/SKaiNET-developers
version: "0.57.0"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/SKaiNET-developers/SKaiNET
url: https://skainet-developers.github.io/SKaiNET/
abstract: >-
  A Kotlin Multiplatform AI framework: tensor operations, a typed
  neural-network DSL for training and inference, autograd, a compiler
  with pluggable CPU/GPU backends, and loaders for GGUF, ONNX, and
  SafeTensors — running natively on JVM, Android, iOS, and embedded
  targets.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - deep learning framework
  - Kotlin Multiplatform
  - tensors
  - neural networks
  - edge inference
  - GGUF
